1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,940
A cafe worker does more than make coffee.

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:11,880
The worker greets the customer, listens to the order, checks the size, asks about milk or sugar, takes payment, makes the drink, and gives the drink to the customer.

3
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:14,720
The customer also has a simple path.

4
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:16,840
First, the customer chooses a drink.

5
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:23,340
Then the customer gives details, like small or medium, hot or iced, and here or to go.

6
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:27,100
After that, the customer pays and waits near the counter.

7
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:30,760
Good cafe English is short and clear.

8
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:33,180
The worker does not need long sentences.

9
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:35,660
The customer needs to feel understood.

10
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:41,080
Coffee names can look difficult, but many cafe orders have simple ideas.

11
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:44,740
An espresso is a very small, strong coffee.

12
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,080
An americano is espresso with hot water.

13
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:52,220
It tastes lighter than espresso, but it is still black coffee.

14
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:56,880
A latte is espresso with a lot of warm milk.

15
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:59,420
It is usually smooth and mild.

16
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:04,200
A cappuccino is espresso with warm milk and more foam on top.

17
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:07,800
It can taste stronger than a latte because it has less milk.

18
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:11,500
An iced coffee is cold coffee with ice.

19
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:15,400
An iced latte is espresso, cold milk, and ice.

20
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:19,400
Some customers also ask for decaf coffee.

21
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:22,520
Decaf means coffee with very little caffeine.

22
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:26,100
Some customers know exactly what they want.

23
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:28,660
Other customers only know the feeling they want.

24
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:33,900
They may say, "I want something not too strong," or "I want something cold and sweet.

25
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:35,460
The worker can help with two questions.

26
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,040
" After that, give one simple suggestion.

27
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,060
Do not list every drink.

28
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:51,660
For example, if the customer wants a mild hot drink, suggest a latte.

29
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:55,960
If the customer wants a cold milk drink, suggest an iced latte.

30
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:59,780
If the customer wants black coffee, suggest an americano.

31
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:02,240
Small problems happen in cafes.

32
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,580
The drink can be wrong.

33
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,180
The milk can be regular milk, but the customer wanted oat milk.

34
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:13,940
The drink can be too hot, too cold, too sweet, or not sweet enough.

35
00:02:14,820 --> 00:02:16,180
The worker should listen first.

36
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,000
" This shows the customer that the worker understands.

37
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,100
Then give a clear next step.

38
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:29,780
The worker can say, "I am sorry.

39
00:02:30,220 --> 00:02:33,240
I can remake it," or "I can add more milk."

40
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:37,060
A calm answer is usually better than a long explanation.
